:: R6_AdrianEntrance [r6 story]
<<scene "Meridian, Floor 40 Event Space" "files/images/characters/r6-adrian-entrance.png">>
<<objective "Meet Adrian Wolfe.">>

I see Victoria first. She's across the room in a black sheath dress and heels that could open mail, talking to a cluster of senior partners with the easy authority of someone who considers herself their equal and might be right. Her posture is immaculate. Her jawline could cut a deal in half. She catches my eye across the crowd and there's a flicker, a micro-expression that lives somewhere between possession and amusement, before her attention returns to the conversation.

Then the room tilts.

I feel it before I see it. The way conversations pause for half a beat. The way heads turn, not dramatically, not all at once, but in a subtle coordinated wave like grass bending under wind. I follow the turning heads and there he is.

Adrian Wolfe.

Victoria introduces him to the room, or maybe the room introduces itself to him. He arrives late but it doesn't read as rude. It reads as unbothered, as though time is a social construct he's chosen to participate in selectively. He's tall. Six-two, maybe six-three. Broad through the shoulders in a way that fills his dark blazer without straining it. Mixed heritage, green eyes that catch the warm event lighting and throw it back brighter. No tie, top button undone, showing a triangle of brown skin at his throat.

He's not the best-dressed person in the room. He's not the loudest. He just occupies space differently. Like gravity is optional for him and he's chosen to stay on the ground as a courtesy.

I watch him move through the crowd. He shakes hands and people lean into him. He speaks and people tilt forward. He laughs and it's easy, genuine, the laugh of a man who finds the world more amusing than threatening. I can see it happening from twenty feet away: people want to be near him. Not sexually. Not professionally. They want to be near him the way you want to stand near a fireplace in December. He radiates warmth you didn't know you needed until you feel it.

Victoria brings him to me briefly.

<<say "Victoria Cross">>Adrian, this is Daniel Ashford. He runs the Tattersall portfolio.<</say>>

Adrian's handshake is nothing like Martin Crane's. No compression, no contest. Just firm and warm and exactly long enough. His green eyes meet mine and I get the strangest sensation, like being seen through. Not scanned. Not evaluated. //Seen//. Like he already knows something about me that I don't, and he finds it interesting.

<<say "Adrian Wolfe">>Daniel. Victoria speaks highly of you.<</say>>

His voice is a low tenor. The kind that carries without effort.

<<sayself>>She's generous.<</sayself>>

<<say "Adrian Wolfe">>She's many things. Generous isn't usually the first adjective.<</say>>

He smiles. It's conspiratorial. I smile back because the alternative is running.

He moves on. I watch him go and realize I'm holding my wine glass too tight, the stem pressing a line into my palm. My cock is half-hard in the panties for reasons I refuse to examine.

Then he finds Lena.

<<npc "adrian" "awareness" 5>>
